Bit-exact OpenCL port of butteraugli, applied to google/guetzli 214f2bb.

The port itself lives outside the submodule, in ../opencl/. This patch is only
the three hooks it cannot live without:

  butteraugli.h                 declares ButteraugliComparator::GpuState (an
                                opaque handle to the device-resident mirror of
                                pi0_) and the destructor that owns it.

  butteraugli.cc                defines GpuState, uploads pi0_ once in the
                                constructor, and routes
                                DiffmapOpsinDynamicsImage through clba:: when a
                                GPU is present. Also adds namespace testhooks,
                                which exposes the file-static stages so
                                ../opencl/clba_test.cc can compare each of them
                                against its kernel.

  butteraugli_comparator.cc     drops a dead OpsinDynamicsImage() call that
                                upstream computes and never reads.

Nothing here changes what butteraugli computes. The GPU and CPU paths agree bit
for bit as long as the target is built with -ffp-contract=off; see
../opencl/README.md for why that flag is load-bearing.

